.TH SSS_CHAIN 1 "June 2026" "SSS_CHAIN" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sss_chain \- SSS-chaining link generation, validation, and arrangement CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sss_chain
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sss_chain
is a standalone command-line tool for the
.BR sss_chain
Rust crate: forward-only Shamir-style chained links over \( Z_{2^31-1} \)
(default M31 field). Layer 1 provides information-theoretic backward
underdetermination; root secrecy (Layer 2) depends on operator-chosen root
material (not chain length).
.PP
Chains are exchanged in the text
.B .ssc
format (pipe-friendly). Path arguments may be
.B -
for stdin or stdout.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B generate
Build a chain from
.BR --root
and write
.B .ssc
to
.BR --out .
.TP
.B validate
Verify a
.B .ssc
file against
.BR --root .
Exit 0 prints VALID; exit 1 on failure.
.TP
.B arrange
Sort shuffled links (indices 0..n-1), validate pairs, write sorted
.BR .ssc .
.TP
.B depth
Check link at
.BR --index
against link index-1; print depth on success.
.TP
.B demo
Write a deterministic four-link demo chain.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-root " PATH"
Root passphrase or secret bytes. Default
.B -
(read stdin) for
.BR generate .
.TP
.BI \-\-link-byte-len " N"
Bytes per link (minimum 8). Default 16.
.TP
.BI \-\-link-count " N"
Number of links (mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-total-bytes ).
.TP
.BI \-\-total-bytes " N"
Total chain memory; must be divisible by
.BR \-\-link-byte-len .
.TP
.BI \-\-in " PATH"
Input
.B .ssc
file or
.B -
.TP
.BI \-\-out " PATH"
Output path or
.B -
(default stdout).
.TP
.BI \-\-index " N"
Link index for
.B depth
(\( N \>= 1 \)).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Status on stderr only; validate suppresses VALID on stdout.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Show usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate ten links from stdin root:
.PP
.RS
echo -n "my-secret" | sss_chain generate --root - --link-count 10 --out chain.ssc
.RE
.PP
Validate:
.PP
.RS
sss_chain validate --root secret.txt --in chain.ssc
.RE
.PP
Pipe arrange:
.PP
.RS
cat chain.ssc | sss_chain arrange --root secret.txt --in - --out -
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success or VALID chain.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid chain or operation error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH FILES
.I *.ssc
.RS
Text chain format: header (link_byte_len, link_count) and hex-encoded links.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ITS\-OTM_public_attestation (7),
.BR ITS\-self_enclosed_timelock (7)
